.TH COSMOLITH 1 "2026-08-09" "cosmolith 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cosmolith \- apply COSMIC configuration changes to a running Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cosmolith
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cosmolith
is a long-running daemon that watches COSMIC configuration changes and applies
the supported changes to the running Wayland compositor through its IPC
interface. It also sends the current input configuration when it starts.
.PP
The compositor backend is selected from the current session. The package
supports Hyprland, Sway, KDE, and GNOME backends; only events implemented by
the selected backend are applied.
.SH INVOCATION
Run
.B cosmolith
from the active graphical session. The program takes no documented command-line
options or arguments.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only the configuration events implemented by the selected compositor backend
are applied. Unsupported events may be logged or ignored. If no supported
compositor is detected, configuration events are logged but are not applied.
The compositor must already be running and expose the IPC interface required by
its backend.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cosmic-config (1)
.SH AUTHORS
